From 60487e13b107fbc509d98dda6ab44fe7284b894a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David <amegahurt@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 14:14:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Fix MSVC build: neutralize Windows min/max macros in
 collision_detector

The macOS port converted collision_detector.cpp's bare min()/max() calls to
std::min/std::max so they resolve without the Windows min/max macros. On MSVC
those macros are still defined (rigid_body_system.h includes <Windows.h> with
no NOMINMAX), so std::max(...) macro-expands to std::(...) -> C2589/C2059.

A project-wide NOMINMAX isn't safe here: yds_ds8_audio_source.cpp (Windows-only
DirectSound) legitimately relies on the min/max macros. Undefine them locally in
this translation unit instead, which now uses the std:: forms. Restores the
Windows build; no effect on the macOS/Clang build.

(cherry picked from commit ae1d929aebd836b02d069e28a4748d35ebb0af5f)
---
 physics/src/collision_detector.cpp | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/physics/src/collision_detector.cpp b/physics/src/collision_detector.cpp
index d02b75fd..aea4f00c 100644
--- a/physics/src/collision_detector.cpp
+++ b/physics/src/collision_detector.cpp
@@ -4,6 +4,17 @@
 #include <math.h>
 #include <algorithm>
 
+// <Windows.h> (pulled in transitively via rigid_body.h) defines min/max as
+// macros on MSVC, which mangle the std::min/std::max calls below. Undefine
+// them for this translation unit so the qualified calls compile on Windows
+// as they do on Clang/macOS.
+#ifdef min
+#undef min
+#endif
+#ifdef max
+#undef max
+#endif
+
 #define THRESH_0_POSITIVE 10e-9
 #define THRESH_0_NEGATIVE (-THRESH_0_POSITIVE)
 
